+# Wynn-Photon settings
 
+option.WYNN_PHOTON_INFO                = Wynn-Photon
+value.WYNN_PHOTON_INFO.0               = §aWynncraft block tweaks
+option.WYNN_PHOTON_INFO.comment        = Wynn-Photon patches Photon for Wynncraft's resource pack. These settings tune its block changes. The strengths scale both the glow and the light the block casts, in Colored Lights and in Photonics
+option.WYNN_EMERALD_GLOW               = Emerald Glow
+option.WYNN_EMERALD_GLOW.comment       = Emerald blocks glow faintly green, and emerald ore glows in its green specks. Both cast a faint green light
+option.WYNN_EMERALD_GLOW_I             = Emerald Glow Strength
+option.WYNN_EMERALD_GLOW_I.comment     = Brightness of the emerald glow and its light
+option.WYNN_CHEST_GLOW                 = Chest Glow
+option.WYNN_CHEST_GLOW.comment         = Chests glow faintly, so they are easier to spot in dark caves. With Photonics they also cast a faint warm light. (Colored Lights can't see chests, because they are block entities)
+option.WYNN_CHEST_GLOW_I               = Chest Glow Strength
+option.WYNN_CHEST_GLOW_I.comment       = Brightness of the chest glow and its light
+option.WYNN_CANDLE_LIGHT_I             = Candle Light Strength
+option.WYNN_CANDLE_LIGHT_I.comment     = Brightness of Wynncraft's candle sconces and candelabras: their flames and their light. 0 turns them off
+option.WYNN_MAGMA_GLOW_I               = Magma Glow Strength
+option.WYNN_MAGMA_GLOW_I.comment       = Brightness of the glowing cracks in magma and molten rock, and their light. 0 turns them off
+option.WYNN_ENCHANTING_GLOW_I          = Enchanting Table Glow Strength
+option.WYNN_ENCHANTING_GLOW_I.comment  = Brightness of the enchanting table's faint blue light and its softly glowing blue inlay. Wynncraft places them next to item identifiers. 0 turns them off
+option.WYNN_VANILLA_LIGHT_I             = Light Block Strength
+option.WYNN_VANILLA_LIGHT_I.comment     = Lights blocks from the vanilla lightmap where Colored Lights and Photonics see no light source. Wynncraft lights many caves and rooms with invisible light blocks, which neither light system can see. It fades out on open, sky-lit ground during the day, as in vanilla, but stays in caves. 0 turns it off
+option.WYNN_PHOTONICS_SKY_FILL_I        = Photonics Sky Fill
+option.WYNN_PHOTONICS_SKY_FILL_I.comment = Only with Photonics. Photonics replaces Photon's sky light with its traced bounce light, which is very dim in shade, forests and under overhangs. This adds Photon's own sky light back where the traced light is weaker. 1.00 makes shade as bright as without Photonics. 0 turns it off
+option.WYNN_MIN_LIGHT_I                 = Minimum Light
+option.WYNN_MIN_LIGHT_I.comment         = The least light any surface gets, so nights, dense cities and caves never go fully black. It fades away where other light is brighter, so daylight and lit rooms don't change. Higher values show more detail in the dark but look flatter. 0 turns it off
+option.WYNN_METEORS                      = Meteors
+option.WYNN_METEORS.comment              = Shooting stars cross the night sky, as meteors have fallen on Gavel for two thousand years. Most are white, some blue, a few purple, and red and yellow ones are very rare. They reflect in water
+option.WYNN_METEOR_RATE                  = Meteor Rate
+option.WYNN_METEOR_RATE.comment          = How often shooting stars and fireballs fall. At 1.00 a shooting star falls about every 25 seconds, somewhere in the sky
+option.WYNN_METEOR_SHOWERS               = Meteor Showers
+option.WYNN_METEOR_SHOWERS.comment       = On a rare night the sky fills with shooting stars, all falling away from one point. Needs Meteors
+option.WYNN_FIREBALLS                    = Fireballs
+option.WYNN_FIREBALLS.comment            = Now and then a large, slow meteor with a long glowing tail crosses the sky. Needs Meteors
+option.WYNN_PLAYER_LIGHT_I               = Player Light
+option.WYNN_PLAYER_LIGHT_I.comment       = The player lights their surroundings as if always holding a torch, like the light radius in Diablo. 1.00 is as bright as a torch; higher is brighter and reaches further. A torch or lantern you really hold counts towards it. It casts no shadows. 0 turns it off
